---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Legal from '../components/Legal.astro';
---
<Base title="Privacy notice" description="How compound. collects and uses personal data.">
  <Legal title="Privacy notice" updated="[date]">
    <p>This notice explains how [legal company name] (“compound.”, “we”), company number [number], registered at [address], uses personal data when you visit this website or contact us. We are the data controller.</p>
    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Details you send us through the contact form or a booking: name, work email, company, website, revenue range and your message.</li>
      <li>Basic website usage data, only if you accept analytics cookies (see our <a href="/cookies">cookie policy</a>).</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Why we use it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To reply to your enquiry and arrange a call (our legitimate interest in responding to you).</li>
      <li>To deliver services if you become a client (to perform our contract).</li>
      <li>To understand how the website is used, with your consent.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
    <p>Our website host (Netlify), our booking tool [Cal.com / Calendly], our CRM [HubSpot] and our email provider [provider]. They process data on our instructions. Some may store data outside the UK under approved safeguards.</p>
    <h2>Client data in our diagnostic work</h2>
    <p>When we analyse a client’s business data, we work under a data processing agreement with that client. Customer emails are pseudonymised before analysis and data is deleted or returned when the engagement ends.</p>
    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>Enquiries we don’t take forward are deleted after [12] months. Client records are kept for [6] years for legal and accounting reasons.</p>
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>You can ask to see, correct or delete your data, or object to how we use it, by emailing [email]. You can also complain to the Information Commissioner’s Office at ico.org.uk.</p>
  </Legal>
</Base>
